Subject: [PATCH] wineandroid.drv: Do not stall presents while a window has no surface.

Creating a Vulkan surface waited up to two seconds for Java to deliver
the window's Android surface. A hidden window gets none until it is
shown, and DXVK tries to create the surface again on every present, so
each present of a hidden window blocked for two seconds. Chromium's GPU
process draws all of Steam's windows, so the whole UI crawled and Steam
killed the main window's browser as unresponsive, leaving it black.
Wait at most 50 ms.
---
--- a/dlls/wineandroid.drv/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/wineandroid.drv/vulkan.c
@@ -95,8 +95,11 @@
     }
 
     /* Java creates the client surface asynchronously; until then the window answers -EAGAIN,
-     * which makes libvulkan's connect fail with VK_ERROR_NATIVE_WINDOW_IN_USE_KHR */
-    for (int i = 0, value; i < 200; i++)
+     * which makes libvulkan's connect fail with VK_ERROR_NATIVE_WINDOW_IN_USE_KHR. Give it a
+     * moment, but no more: a hidden window gets no surface until it is shown, and DXVK tries
+     * again on each present, so a long wait stalled every present (Chromium's GPU process
+     * draws all of Steam's windows, and Steam killed them as unresponsive) */
+    for (int i = 0, value; i < 5; i++)
     {
         if (surface->window->query( surface->window, NATIVE_WINDOW_DEFAULT_WIDTH, &value ) != -EAGAIN) break;
         usleep( 10000 );
